00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:22.840
Wait, but I smell gas.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:23.420
Gas?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.940
Gas? I know it's gas.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:27.030
Got your passkey?

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:28.010
Downstairs.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:28.550
Well, get it.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:29.910
Go back.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:39.790
It isn't just something that was going to happen.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:40.390
I told you.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:42.000
I told you.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:43.680
I knew it.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.130
I knew this would happen.

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:49.670
Perfectly all right.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:51.010
Come on, let's get her out of here.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.260
Oh, will you look at that door?

00:15:58.400 --> 00:15:59.980
The landlady will absolutely check.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.340
Help me.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:01.940
Bye.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:05.280
What'd I tell you?

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:07.950
She wants to see me first thing in the morning, see Oli Ho.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.970
You know, I wish you'd do me a favor and stop saving my life.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.180
Well, why can't you find yourself another hobby?

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:18.820
Why don't you take up stamp collecting?

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:24.320
I want a cup of coffee.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:25.860
Don't you think it's too late?

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.560
Oh, it's too late for a lot of things.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:30.600
at

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.310
That dumb lieutenant with all these funny questions.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.000
It was an accident.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:37.240
It was.

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:41.050
I don't say, of course, like that.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.570
If I was going to kill myself, I wouldn't do it with a lot of smelly gas.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.100
Besides, I'm always having accidents.

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:49.400
A couple of nights ago, I fell asleep with a cigarette in my mouth,

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:50.420
burned a hole in the blanket.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:52.320
Well, wait till Mr. Summer sees that.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.380
You must be more careful.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:54.020
Bye.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.680
Couldn't the world struggle along without me? I mean, if it really tried.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:02.300
Made you stop by tonight, anyhow.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:03.280
Want to see how you were.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:04.440
No change.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:05.060
Still loud.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:07.290
Get that job as a camera girl.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:08.280
No.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:09.940
Don't you read the papers?

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:12.350
the more of the famous Wazinski luck.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:14.740
That very night, some hold-up guys shot up the place.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.140
Now they're closed down for repairs.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.080
Thank you.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:19.330
Better get a job in a place where there's so much danger.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:20.520
Danger.

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:23.210
You shouldn't. You really shouldn't. You shouldn't.

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:26.020
Look, Mr. Stern, you just gave me some blood.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.080
You didn't adopt me.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:29.210
I'm sorry.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.220
Oh, I'm sorry, too.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:37.320
It's just that I'm not used to having somebody worry about me.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:38.240
It makes me nervous.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:42.860
I have an idea.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:45.340
What?

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.760
I'm a tax accountant, you know.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:48.200
So?

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:50.500
Can you type?

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:53.800
I'm hardly the secretarial type.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.310
Well, really, it doesn't matter very much.

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:57.390
I mean, if you can print carefully with pen and ink.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:58.810
You offering me a job?

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:00.660
Yes.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:02.610
Why?

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.310
I'll do a sort of responsibility for you.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:12.220
Why?

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:14.980
Just do.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.330
You really mean that, don't you?

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:20.030
Yes.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.040
We're crying out loud.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:25.240
Look, it would be easy.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:26.960
You could move into my house and then we...

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:27.320
Oh!

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:31.400
Bye-bye.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:34.530
Please don't misunderstand me.

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:37.060
You see, it's not a very big house.

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.730
But there's plenty of room I could sleep in the attic or even get a room next door.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.460
I just thought it would be easier.

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:44.460
Will you do it?

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:50.520
like to help you.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:56.280
I sure don't have any better office, and it'd be a pleasure to get out of this dump.

00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:58.530
Thank you, Ms. Lynn.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:01.150
Wyszynski.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:05.260
Wyszynski.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.610
I thought guys like you went out of style a couple of centuries ago.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.770
Martha, I told you not to go swimming so soon after lunch.

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:20.820
Well, you asked me not to do so many things, I lost track.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.540
Besides, I was only kidding. I'm a fool here, too.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.610
Your friend looked a little upset. I thought I'd make like a hero.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.880
Why should I be upset? Thank you very much, young man.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.530
For what? Big laugh, I swim ten times better than he does.

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.160
Oh yeah? Prove it.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:38.230
Please don't go in, you might get a cramp. Go under.

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:42.710
This don't do this, don't do that routine is beginning to bug me. Now will you let go?

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.580
Martha, please don't go in.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.030
You're getting a little bored with being treated like a six-year-old child, Mr. Sturm.

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:13.650
My grandpa forgot my key.

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:15.750
You remember old Fearless Fosdick?

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:16.720
Where were you?

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:18.500
We went for a drive.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.000
Fearless and me went for a little drive.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:22.760
You're both drunk.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:26.430
One hundred percent super duper trooper drunk.

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:28.350
What are you doing driving when you're drunk?

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:29.850
Don't you know it's dangerous?

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:31.560
You want to end up in the morgue?

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:33.840
Worry, worry, worry.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:36.060
You know, you're like a little old lady sitting in a rocking chair,

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.100
worrying about this and worrying about that.

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:39.780
Get out.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.640
Just a cotton-picking second, Grandpa.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:45.640
I did something wrong.

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:47.830
I do more things wrong.

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:48.910
Go to bed!

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:50.880
Wait outside.

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:52.390
Maybe I ought to go.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:53.790
You better wait outside.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:57.620
Okay, Gramps.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:11.890
Going out of your way to put yourself in danger?

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:16.590
What big teeth you have, Grandpa!

00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:32.980
Marta, I'm sorry.

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:34.120
Do you believe it?

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:36.520
At first I got a bang out of this kindergarten routine.

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:39.140
Marta, if you'd only listen to me, perhaps I could explain.

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:40.580
Oh, Mr. Sterling.

00:22:40.910 --> 00:22:42.640
All right, I'll show you.

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:55.890
Marta, I want you to look at these,

00:22:55.910 --> 00:22:57.470
and then you'll understand what I'm trying to say.

00:22:58.120 --> 00:22:59.260
Marta, please look at these.

00:22:59.400 --> 00:22:59.980
I can't let it happen.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.290
to you every one of them i knew what was going to happen to every one of them both the good and

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:08.940
the bad marta i know what's going to happen to you so do i i'm leaving unless we do something to

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.300
prevent it marty you're going to die in a terrible way now knock it off will you believe me i know

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:19.880
marta are you coming or not he's waiting for me if you go with this young man something will happen

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:24.140
i know it will martha please look at these will you please stop acting like this it's embarrassing

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:27.620
don't you think i know why you're doing it what are you talking about oh at first i thought it

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:29.460
It was cute, but who's kidding who, Mr. Stern?

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:29.900
You're 20.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:34.360
five years older than I am. What do you mean? You know what I mean. Stop acting like that. What do

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:46.420
you mean? What are you talking about? You must believe me. You just must believe me. Marta died

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:53.570
violently, fulfilling Harold Stern's prophecy, though certainly not as he'd expected. A few

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:59.240
months later, Mr. Stern passed away in an asylum for the criminally insane, and there the matter

00:23:59.240 --> 00:23:59.540
ended.

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:04.290
And yet there are those who still speculate about his fantastic power of clairvoyance,

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:07.850
the woman who unexpectedly inherited a great fortune,

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:13.520
or his intuition that took him to Marta's room before the gas could kill her.

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:17.370
To explain it, we cannot. We can only wonder.

00:24:18.280 --> 00:24:22.450
Another enigma in the world that thus far remains one step beyond.
